# What must NOT reach the Docker build context.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not hygiene. Without it two things go wrong, and
# the second one breaks the build:
#
# 1. The context is ~366 MB — .git, backend/.venv, frontend/node_modules, the
#    developer's var/*.db files and .env — all uploaded to the daemon on every
#    build, and .env is a secret that has no business being in a build context.
#
# 2. `COPY frontend/ ./` runs *after* `npm ci`, so the host's node_modules
#    overwrites the one just installed. On a macOS host that means
#    @esbuild/darwin-arm64 and @rollup/rollup-darwin-arm64 land in a linux
#    image. The layer-caching intent — dependencies first, sources second — is
#    defeated at the same time.
#
# Note the asymmetry with .gitignore: deploy/wheels/*.whl is git-ignored and
# must be *present* here, because the AlphaLab wheel is not on PyPI and the
# image cannot be built without it.

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- the developer's own data ------------------------------------------------
var/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- installed dependencies and build output --------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
frontend/dist
backend/build
backend/dist
**/*.egg-info

# --- caches and bytecode -----------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- history and tooling -----------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude

# --- not needed at runtime ---------------------------------------------------
# The image runs the application; it does not run the suite. Tests reach the
# image through CI, which runs them before anything is built.
backend/tests
docs
scripts
README.md

# --- editors / os ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
